---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Market overview"
  description="Where the S&P 500 is, how fast it is moving, which regime it is in, how unstable that regime is, and the distribution of where it could go — read live from the FinDynamics API."
  eyebrow="FinDynamics"
  heading="Where the market is"
  intro="Position, velocity, regime, instability and a distribution — not a target. Every number here is estimated from information that was available on its own date, and every one of them links to the page that shows how it was built."
>
  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="now-h">
    <div class="panel__head">
      <h2 id="now-h">Right now</h2>
      <span class="panel__note">/api/v1/state &middot; /api/v1/instability</span>
    </div>
    <p class="prose">
      The four readings that the whole system exists to produce: which regime the market is in and
      how confident the model is, how fast the filtered level is moving, how close the regime looks
      to changing, and whether the system would transmit a shock. Each is a link into
      <a href="/equity">FinEquity</a>, where the same number appears with its full derivation.
    </p>
    <div class="tiles" id="overview-now" style="margin-top:0.85rem"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="crash-h">
    <div class="panel__head">
      <h2 id="crash-h">Crash risk, decomposed</h2>
      <span class="panel__note">FINDYN_V1_SPEC.md &sect;4</span>
    </div>
    <p class="prose">
      Never one number. A market that may turn without breaking and a market that is fine until it
      is not produce the same composite and call for opposite responses, so the three factors are
      published together and the product only beside them.
    </p>
    <div id="overview-crash" style="margin-top:0.85rem"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="fan-h">
    <div class="panel__head">
      <h2 id="fan-h">Where it could go</h2>
      <span class="panel__note">/api/v1/forecast</span>
    </div>
    <p class="prose">
      Quantile bands from at least ten thousand simulated paths per horizon, conditioned on
      today&rsquo;s regime posterior. There is no point estimate here and there is no
      <em>&ldquo;S&amp;P at X&rdquo;</em> anywhere in this system &mdash; the table these are stored
      in has no column for one.
    </p>
    <div id="overview-forecast" style="margin-top:0.85rem"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="engines-h">
    <div class="panel__head">
      <h2 id="engines-h">Engines</h2>
      <span class="panel__note">/api/v1/assets</span>
    </div>
    <p class="prose">
      One card per registered engine, read from the registry rather than from whatever happens to be
      in the database &mdash; an engine that has shipped but not yet run says so instead of
      disappearing. Serving-plane health, ingestion sources and the endpoint contract live on
      <a href="/status">system status</a>.
    </p>
    <div id="engines" style="margin-top:0.85rem"></div>
  </section>
</Base>

<script>
  import '../scripts/overview';
  import { mountEngines } from '../scripts/engines';

  void mountEngines('#engines');
</script>
